# Build-context rules for the API image (root Dockerfile). BuildKit uses this file
# instead of .dockerignore for that Dockerfile, so it repeats the shared rules and
# adds `apps`, which the API image never needs. Keep the two files in sync.
#
# The context is what `COPY . .` copies, and every copied file ends up in an image
# layer for good. Nothing below belongs in an image: secrets, customer documents,
# keys and local build output. Patterns use `**/` so they apply at any depth
# (a bare `.env` only matches the repository root, which let packages/api/.env.local
# and apps/web/.env.local into the image).

# VCS and tooling
.git
.claude
.agents
.turbo
**/.turbo
.vercel
**/.vercel
**/.next
**/node_modules
patches

# Build output and caches
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/app-export
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/*.log

# Secrets (the example file stays: it holds no values)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/keystore.properties
**/keystore_base64.txt

# Customer data and release artifacts that may exist on a server checkout.
# Only the bundled demo images under uploads/seed ship with the API.
packages/api/uploads/*
!packages/api/uploads/seed
**/storage
**/*.sql
**/*.apk
**/*.aab
**/*.zip

# Not needed to build or run either image
docs
tools
apps
